{"data":{"updated_timestamp":"12/11/2026 13:22:03","profile":{"player_id":"106862","last_updated":"12/11/2026 13:22","fullname":"Palle Kankanamage Malki Madara","short_display_name":"M Madara","name":"Malki Madara","gender":"F","dob":"30/12/2000","date_of_death":null,"place_birth":"Sri Lanka","nationality_id":"8","nationality":"Sri Lanka","nationality_short_code":"SL","nick_name":null,"player_skill":{"id":"2","text":"Bowler","role":"Bowler"},"batting_style":{"id":"1","text":"Right Handed"},"bowling_style":{"id":"11","text":"Right-arm medium"},"writeup":"<p>Malki Madara is a talented Sri Lankan cricketer born on December 30, 2000, who has been making waves in the cricket world with her impressive skills as a right-arm medium-fast bowler. Her journey to international cricket began in  February 2025 when she earned her maiden call-up to the Sri Lanka women's  national team for the ODI and T20I series against New Zealand.</p>\r\n<p><br />\r\nShe made her T20I debut on March 14, 2025, against New Zealand, impressively taking three wickets and earning the Player of the Match award. This early success was followed by her ODI debut against India on April 27, 2025, in the  Tri-Nation series. Madara continued to shine, taking four wickets against South  Africa on May 2, 2025, in her second international match.</p>\r\n<p><br />\r\nWith her exceptional bowling skills and growing experience, Madara is poised to become a key player for Sri Lanka's national side. Her ability to adapt to different formats and opposition makes her a valuable asset to the team. As she continues to gain more experience and fine-tune her skills, fans can expect to see more impressive performances from this talented young cricketer.<br />\r\n&nbsp;</p>","relation":null,"social_details":null,"trophy_cabinet":null,"majorteams":{"team":[{"id":"1133","active":"1","is_primary":"true","is_international":"1","text":"Sri Lanka"},{"id":"3759","active":"1","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"SLC B